                "Two yardsticks. **P/E** compares the share price with profit after tax. **EV/EBITDA** compares the value of the whole business (market value plus debt, minus cash) with operating profit, so it gives credit for cash and charges for debt. **For the coworking companies, use P/E on filed profit**: their EV/EBITDA looks cheap only because lease accounting inflates EBITDA, and Screener's net debt for them is mostly future rent.",
