        body: [
            "**Staffing and facility services.** **Quess Corp: follow**; the best mix and balance sheet among the people businesses, but the tax disputes, the cut headcount target and a price that needs more than my ~10% argue for patience. **TeamLease Services: follow**; cheap and cash-rich, but it has dropped its target and carries PF claims. **Krystal Integrated Services: wait**, now a turnaround that must recover its loans and its rating. **Updater Services: wait** for clean quarters and a clear use of its cash.",
            "**Specialist services.** **CMS Info Systems: own**, a cash-rich leader priced for slow growth, though it must stop cutting revenue guidance. **MSTC**, **Redington** and **Sanghvi Movers: follow**; MSTC for its mandate once the audit and coal questions clear, Redington once its price-led boom settles, Sanghvi once the Saudi cranes are earning.",
            "**Office space.** **Nirlon: follow** for its dividend. **Awfis Space Solutions: follow**, judged on its cash margin after rent and bought only on weakness. **EFC (I): wait**; the cheapest here, but its governance and cash conversion must improve first. **WeWork India**, **Indiqube Spaces** and **Smartworks Coworking: wait** for filed profits that support their prices.",
            "**What would change my view.** For the better: flex operators' filed profit after tax catching up with their adjusted figures; Redington turning profit into cash; favourable rulings in Quess's and TeamLease's tax and PF cases. For the worse: a slowdown in GCC hiring that empties desks while new supply arrives; the first coal exchange opening (MSTC); PC prices falling with channel stock still high (Redington).",
            "**What to watch next quarter.** Quess's net adds; CMS's public-sector price rises; MSTC's FY27 credit-loss policy; Redington's festive demand and cash; TeamLease's H2 margin; Nirlon's dividend; Sanghvi's Saudi cranes; EFC's cash; Awfis's cash EBITDA; Krystal's loans and rating; Updater's cash use; WeWork India's pledge; Indiqube's audited cash flow; Smartworks' mega-campus occupancy.",
        ],
        bottomLine:
            "Own the cash-rich leader priced for slow growth (CMS Info Systems); follow the growing, cash-rich or high-yield names (Quess Corp, MSTC, Redington, TeamLease Services, Nirlon, Sanghvi Movers, Awfis Space Solutions); and wait on the rest (EFC (I), Krystal Integrated Services, Updater Services, WeWork India, Indiqube Spaces, Smartworks Coworking) until filed profits and cleaner governance catch up.",
